    "rootCause": "The bundled Paddle-Lite crashes (SIGSEGV / SEGV_ACCERR in a conv worker thread, pc 0xc7a44 / 0xc7a40 / 0xc7930 / 0x11f2cc in libpaddle_light_api_shared.so) when the FIRST detector run of a process has a short input after DetResizeImg (1000x320 -> 256x960, 640x320 -> 320x640, 1000x300 -> 288x960 ...). Once a large shape (1000x640 -> 576x960, reference 608x928, or 960x960) has run first, every later shape passes. The earlier size sweep looked size-dependent only because crashed processes restarted and the passing sizes ran in a warmed process.",
